; Test whether an object is within an observer's reach
;
; The object (IY, id in A) must be present (flag bit 7). It is within reach when
; the observer (IX) is itself inside that object (the first holder in the
; observer's chain that is not open or alive, see #R$9E7A, is the object), or
; when both have the same such closed holder: if that holder is a real one
; they are inside it together, and if it is $FF (both out in the open) the
; observer's first location must be one of the object's locations.
;
; A Id of the object at IY
; IX Record of the observer (an actor or the player)
; IY Record of the object
; O:F NZ when the object is within reach, Z when not (or when it is not present)
@label=CanReach
@isub=BIT FLAG_PRESENT,(IY+$07)
c$9E40 BIT 7,(IY+$07)
 $9E44 RET Z
 $9E45 PUSH IY
 $9E47 PUSH IX
 $9E49 PUSH BC
 $9E4A LD B,A           ; B = object id
 $9E4B LD C,(IX+$10)    ; C = location of the observer
 $9E4E PUSH IY
 $9E50 CALL $9E7A       ; closed holder of the observer
 $9E53 CP B             ; the object itself? then reachable
 $9E54 LD B,A
 $9E55 POP IX
 $9E57 JR Z,$9E72
 $9E59 CALL $9E7A       ; closed holder of the object
 $9E5C CP B             ; must be the observer's
 $9E5D JR NZ,$9E6F
 $9E5F INC A            ; $FF + 1 = 0: both in the open
 $9E60 JR NZ,$9E72
 $9E62 LD B,(IY+$00)    ; B = number of locations of the object
 $9E65 LD A,C
@label=CanReach_Location
*$9E66 CP (IY+$10)
 $9E69 JR Z,$9E72
 $9E6B INC IY
 $9E6D DJNZ $9E66
*$9E6F XOR A
 $9E70 JR $9E74
*$9E72 OR $01
*$9E74 POP BC
 $9E75 POP IX
 $9E77 POP IY
 $9E79 RET
